I am staying with a music loving friend and we have spent an evening listening to music on his Bose speaker set up. Soundtouch 300 with sub and 2 tweeters. Cost him close to £1000 apparently. 🤷‍♂️ While it fills the room very well and has a big sound, plenty of rumble, it left me missing the details in so many songs. It was just too bloated and muddy for my taste. He loves it and I have no issues with that. Sound is always subjective and if you like a sound, it's a good sound. Firm believer in that so I intend no hate here. To be clear, he bought it for his TV first but has also set it up for music too. I've just gone to bed and I'm listening to a set of KZ ZS10 pro through my Fiio KA1 with Wavelet EQ and it blows his set up out of the water for me. At literally less than 10% of the cost all in. There's clarity, crispness, tight responsive bass, engaging sound, the whole package for me and it's just my travel set up. I'm missing my Grado's and AKG's at home! Long story short, I'm so glad I spent some time to explore different tech, advice, sound profiles etc. It's made me fall in love with music all over again and listening to other set ups makes me realize how far I've come! If you're still reading, check out Chromology by Thank You Scientist one you're favourite set up. Well worth a listen. 16